 "max_abs_pooled_minus_mean_other_headline": 0.0005209850864803522,
 "reading": "The pooled OOF AUC ranks rows from five different Platt-scaled models together, so for the SVMs it falls below the mean of the five per-fold AUCs; for every other headline model the two agree to within 0.0005.  The linear SVM's large gap has a visible cause: in every fold 65%-67% of its OOF probabilities lie within 0.002 of a fold-specific floor (0.1227-0.1266), and pooling stacks these near-tied blocks on top of each other.  The 6,000-row figure is the maximum over 18 settings on the subsample's own folds and is not comparable with full-set CV AUCs.  RBF SVM rank among the 11 headline models (others by their per-fold mean CV AUC): subsample_cv_auc 7 (between tree_pruned and logistic); pooled_oof_auc 7 (between tree_pruned and logistic); per_fold_mean_oof_auc 7 (between tree_pruned and logistic)."
}